menu "44net Tester"

config TESTER_AP_SSID
    string "Provisioning AP SSID"
    default "44net-tester-setup"
    help
      SSID raised when no credentials are stored or when joining fails. The
      AP is open by design: it exists only during short recovery windows.

config TESTER_PORTAL_TIMEOUT_S
    int "Portal window before reboot (seconds)"
    default 600
    help
      How long the provisioning portal stays up before rebooting and retrying
      the stored credentials. Bounded on purpose: a transient AP outage must
      not park the device in AP mode forever at a remote site.

config TESTER_STA_MAX_RETRY
    int "Join attempts before falling back to the portal"
    default 3

config TESTER_BOOT_GPIO
    int "GPIO of the BOOT button"
    default 0
    help
      0 on ESP32 and ESP32-S3, 9 on ESP32-C3.

      Held for three seconds DURING OPERATION it erases the stored network and
      reboots into the portal. It is deliberately not read at reset: the ROM
      bootloader samples GPIO0 there and enters serial download mode when it is
      low, so a button checked at reset is invisible to the application.

config TESTER_UDP_PORT
    int "UDP port to listen on"
    default 5000
    help
      Answers test 4 of docs/test-procedure.md, which probes an allowed UDP
      port. Arrivals are recorded (headers only) and shown on the status page.

config TESTER_OTA_ENABLE
    bool "Enable the POST /ota update command"
    default y
    help
      Writes flash. Protect it with a firewall rule scoped to the source
      address of your update host; the token below is a guard against
      mistakes, not against an attacker.

config TESTER_OTA_TOKEN
    string "Bearer token required by POST /ota"
    default "change-me"
    depends on TESTER_OTA_ENABLE

config TESTER_CHECK_44NET
    string "A 44net host to try reaching (blank to skip)"
    default ""
    help
      Answers "can this segment reach 44net at all". Tried on tcp/80.

config TESTER_CHECK_INTERNAL
    string "An internal host that must NOT be reachable (blank to skip)"
    default ""
    help
      Test 7 of docs/test-procedure.md - the rule that makes the segment a DMZ.
      Tried on tcp/80; a result other than "blocked" means your isolation is
      not holding.

config TESTER_CHECK_INTERNET
    string "An internet host to try reaching (blank to skip)"
    default "1.1.1.1"
    help
      Informational: whether the segment has outbound internet. Tried on
      tcp/53. Either answer can be correct depending on how you scoped egress.

endmenu
